# OfficeHub — Cursor rules

Canonical source: read [AGENTS.md](../../AGENTS.md) at repo root before suggesting code.

## Stack (exact versions)
- Next.js 15.1+ (App Router, Server Components, Server Actions)
- TypeScript strict (`@typescript-eslint/strict-type-checked`)
- Postgres 16 + Prisma 5+
- Auth.js v5 (credentials provider, JWT sessions)
- BlockNote 0.31 (SSR-guarded)
- Tailwind 3 + shadcn-style component layer
- Node 20+ / Docker Compose for self-host

## Hard rules
1. Strict TypeScript — never `any`. Use `unknown` + narrowing or Zod schemas.
2. Server actions in `src/app/dashboard/actions.ts` — one file, all mutations.
3. REST routes use `requireApiAuth()` from `src/lib/api.ts`.
4. RBAC via `src/lib/rbac.ts` — every project-touching mutation passes `memberIds` to `canEditProject`.
5. Forms → server actions. API routes → external automation only.
6. BlockNote hooks crash in SSR — always mount-guard (see `src/components/editor/BlockEditor.tsx`).
7. Server actions as props → use `action.bind(null, id)`. Never inline arrows.
8. Server components → use `<AutoSubmitSelect>` instead of `<select onChange>`.
9. Pure white theme — black only as text + thin borders + small icon fills.
10. Validate every input with Zod from `src/lib/validation.ts`.
11. Wrap `useTransition(async)` in try/catch + toast.
12. `revalidatePath` after every mutation.
13. No raw `JSON.parse` — use `parseJSON` helper.

## Permission boundaries (3-tier)

| Action | Allowed |
|---|---|
| **Always** | Add new server action / page / component matching existing patterns · Add Zod schema · Fix typecheck errors · Update tests · Add `revalidatePath` calls |
| **Ask first** | Schema change (new model, new column, new index) · Auth flow change · New external dependency · Removing a public API endpoint · Adding a feature flag |
| **Never** | Skip the typecheck gate · Add `dark:` Tailwind variants (dead code) · Catch + swallow errors silently · Hard-code role checks · Add solid black or colored backgrounds · Commit `.env` or secrets |

## How to add a feature
Follow `docs/EXTENDING.md` (7-step recipe). For larger work: `docs/GSD-PLAYBOOK.md`.

